    "body": "### Added\r\n- `keep_last_tab` is now a tri-state mode (#3):\r\n  - `0` — close the window when the last tab is closed (default Chrome behavior)\r\n  - `1` — keep the window open by opening a new tab (previous on-state)\r\n  - `2` — close the window only when the last remaining tab is an idle new-tab page\r\n- New-tab detection for mode `2` uses the tab title plus an omnibox-focus guard, so it closes only on an idle NTP and never discards in-progress address-bar input."
  },
